                <pb facs="0777" n="657" sameAs="frus:frus1922v01/pg657"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">832.415/16</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Brazilian Ambassador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Alencar</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-02-13"><hi rendition="#italic">February 13,
                        1922</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: I have received
                    instructions from the President of Brazil to invite the Government of the United
                    States <pb facs="0778" n="658" xml:id="pg658"/> to attend the Centennial
                    Celebration of the Independence of Brazil, in September next at Rio de
                    Janeiro.</p>
                <p>I am transmitting to you this invitation by letter, not being able to call on you
                    before your departure tomorrow, confined, as I am, by direction of my physician,
                    to my bed since several days ago, and I do not know for how much longer.</p>
                <p>With the expressions [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">A. de Alencar</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
